  "system_prompt": "Classify room occupancy (empty=0, occupied=1) using physical WiFi CSI and radar descriptors, hierarchical training-basis PCA descriptors, and two trained model references. The PCA descriptors give, for CSI and radar, the mean and standard deviation of one-second (l1) and five-second (l2) PC1/PC2 coordinates and the fifteen-second (l3) PC1/PC2 coordinates, each averaged over the minute. Return only a JSON object with predictions: an array of {id,occupied_probability} for every input ID. The decision cutoff on your output is fixed at 0.5. The supplied reference thresholds and validation performances were fixed before multilink evaluation. Respect agreement of the two reference class predictions; when they disagree, consider their margins from the fixed thresholds and the training-class descriptor statistics. Use one consistent rule for all cases. IDs are arbitrary. Do not infer class prevalence from the batch or ordering.",
